.TH DISPLAY 4 "31 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
display \- which screen X uses on this machine, and how it starts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/display
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B /etc/display
says which display card X runs on, in which mode, and whether a graphical
login starts at boot.
The installer writes it, the administrator edits it, and no package owns it.
.BR xstart (1)
reads it for every session, and the boot step
.B /etc/rc2.d/S95display
for the graphical login.
.PP
Each line is a key and its value, separated by blanks or tabs.
A
.B #
starts a comment that runs to the end of the line; blank lines are ignored.
When a key is given twice, the last line counts.
A key that is missing takes the default given below.
.TP
.BI card " name"
the card, by the name of its file in
.BR /etc/display.d ,
or
.B auto
(the default): the first card whose device answers, in name order, with
.B native
(the chipset display) last.
See
.BR display.d (4).
.TP
.BI mode " W" x H
the screen size, as
.BR 1024x768 ;
it must be one of the card's modes.
Default: the card's first.
A card that picks its own mode (the chipset display) ignores it.
.TP
.BI depth " bits"
the number of bits a pixel; it must be one of the card's depths.
Default: the card's first.
.TP
.B start manual \fR|\fP xdm
.B manual
(the default): X starts only when a user runs
.BR xstart .
.BR xdm :
the graphical login starts at boot, on this card and mode, with X11R6's
.BR xdm ;
the system's own
.B xdm
runs only as a port monitor of the service access facility, set up with
.BR amixadm ,
and is not started from here.
The line
.B display=no
in
.BR /etc/rc.conf
turns the boot step off whatever this says (see
.BR rc.conf (4)).
.TP
.BI session " path"
the session for a user who has neither
.B ~/.xsession
nor
.BR ~/.xinitrc .
Default:
.BR /usr/lib/amix/xsession ,
which starts an
.B xterm
and the first window manager it finds.
.TP
.BI monsw " sum"
for a card that shares the monitor with the chipset display, the monitor
switch: the sum of the bits that say which lines switch it and at which
level (1 CTS, 2 SEL, 16 and 32 their levels; 34 is SEL, the card's picture
when low), the value of the Z3660's own setting.
Absent: the value the card itself offers.
.PP
Every mistake in the file is reported, with its line number, by
.BR "xstart \-n" ;
a line with a mistake is ignored.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.ft CW
# /etc/display
card     auto
mode     1920x1080
start    xdm
monsw    34
.ft R
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/display
this file.
.TP
.B /etc/display.d/*
the cards.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xstart (1),
.BR display.d (4),
.BR rc.conf (4)
